<Project>

  <!--
    THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT IMPORT THE ROOT Directory.Build.props, for the
    same reason src/Ft8Sharp/Directory.Build.props does not (HM-DEC-152).

    MSBuild walks up from a project looking for the first Directory.Build.props and
    stops at it. The usual courtesy is to import the one above before adding to it.
    Not importing it is the whole point here, and the absence of that import is a
    decision rather than an oversight.

    The root file injects Version, and with it AssemblyVersion,
    AssemblyInformationalVersion and BuildStampUtc, into every project in the
    solution. Ft8Sharp.Deep is a library with its own licence, its own NOTICE and
    its own reason to exist, and a library that announces itself as version 1.12.48
    of a desktop program is wrong on the first line a reader of the package sees.
    HM-DEC-063 exists so the tree has one answer to "what version is this app";
    Ft8Sharp.Deep is not the app.

    0.1.0 BECAUSE IT DELEGATES AND NOTHING ELSE.

    Unit 245 creates this library to satisfy step 1 of PHASE_PLAN.md, whose whole
    point is that BEHAVIOUR DOES NOT CHANGE. Ft8DeepSlotDecoder holds an
    Ft8SlotDecoder built with the parameters it was handed and returns that
    decoder's Ft8SlotResult unchanged - every count and every message, in order.
    There is no ordered statistics decoding here, no subtraction, no re-sync, no
    per-message SNR and no cross-slot combining. Those are steps 2 to 6 and not one
    line of any of them is in this version.

    So the scoreboard reads two columns tonight and they agree decode for decode,
    which is a statement about the SEAM and about the harness wiring and about
    nothing else. From the unit that takes step 2, a difference between the columns
    is attributable to exactly one named change, and that is what this version buys.

    A 0.x rather than a 1.x, and the reason is the same as Ft8Sharp's own first
    version: a 1.x would claim a maturity this library has not got. The minor is
    bumped when it gains a capability of its own.

    0.2.0 at unit 246, which is that bump: this library now runs the port's
    per-candidate loop itself and carries an ordered statistics decoder, so it can
    reach codewords the port cannot. What it may NOT do is decide that any of them
    is a message - the port's parity gate and CRC-14 gate remain the only
    acceptance, and there is still no checksum in this library.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>0.2.0</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    AND NO GIT COMMIT EITHER, for the reason recorded beside Ft8Sharp's own copy of
    this property: the SDK appends the repository's source revision to
    AssemblyInformationalVersion by itself, without help from the root file, so
    dropping the inheritance above is not enough on its own.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion>false</IncludeSourceRevisionInInformationalVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
